WEBVTT

00:24.800 --> 00:28.532
Good morning and welcome to our special council meeting on March 4,

00:28.675 --> 00:32.948
2025. The purpose of this meeting is to consider the opt to fill vacant

00:33.044 --> 00:34.160
council position.

00:37.180 --> 00:40.964
I now call on Will Short, Regional Clerk, to conduct the roll call. Thank you,

00:40.972 --> 00:44.196
Chair. Chair Redman. Present. Councillor Craig Councillor.

00:44.228 --> 00:47.828
Erb. Councillor Foxton. Councillor Harris.

00:47.924 --> 00:51.080
Present. Councillor Huinink. Present.

00:51.580 --> 00:54.840
Councillor James. Present. Councillor Liggett.

00:55.340 --> 00:58.448
Councillor McCabe. Councillor Nowak.

00:58.644 --> 01:03.100
Councillor Salonen. Present. Councillor Shantz. Present. Councillor Vrbanovic.

01:03.520 --> 01:06.984
Councillor Williams. Councillor Wolf. Present.

01:07.072 --> 01:10.904
Thank you, Chair. I'd like to acknowledge that

01:10.912 --> 01:14.648
the land on which we gather today is the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee,

01:14.664 --> 01:18.504
the Anishinaabe and the Chonnonton peoples. In doing so, I want to

01:18.512 --> 01:21.944
reflect on what it means to be doing important community work like we're engaging

01:21.992 --> 01:25.512
in collectively today. And also in my own relationship to the

01:25.536 --> 01:29.272
land as a settler. One of the most important aspects of my

01:29.296 --> 01:33.160
individual journey towards truth and reconciliation has been to listen.

01:33.320 --> 01:36.632
I am constantly grateful to the community that shares their stories

01:36.696 --> 01:39.784
and their concerns with me, as well as the chair of

01:39.792 --> 01:43.432
the region. I know I carry a large responsibility to ensure that it is not

01:43.456 --> 01:46.824
just myself on an individual level, listening and acting,

01:46.952 --> 01:50.088
but that as a government, we are listening and creating action in the

01:50.144 --> 01:54.200
community. I offer this acknowledgement as one of the many actions I am

01:54.240 --> 01:57.884
personally in the region largely is taking in our journey towards

01:57.992 --> 02:02.084
reconciliation. We recognize the enduring presence of the Indigenous

02:02.132 --> 02:05.860
peoples with whom we share this land today, their achievements and their

02:05.900 --> 02:09.364
contributions to our community. Are there any declarations

02:09.412 --> 02:13.120
of pecuniary interest under the Municipal Conflict of Interest Act?

02:15.180 --> 02:18.360
Seeing none. Are there any delegations?

02:20.060 --> 02:23.860
Seeing none. I would now

02:23.900 --> 02:26.480
call on Will Short to introduce a report.

02:27.460 --> 02:31.036
Thank you. Chair to Council, good morning.

02:31.108 --> 02:34.844
You will remember on our last committee day in February, we briefly

02:34.892 --> 02:38.412
discussed the vacancy

02:38.476 --> 02:42.156
report when we actually let everybody know about Councillor Deutschmann's

02:42.188 --> 02:45.640
resignation. At the time, council requested to

02:45.940 --> 02:48.956
defer the report until following the provincial election,

02:49.028 --> 02:51.280
which happened on February 27th.

02:51.780 --> 02:55.234
So it's the same report that we were working on at

02:55.242 --> 02:58.658
the time. It outlines the options for either

02:58.834 --> 03:02.562
filling the vacancy through an appointment by

03:02.586 --> 03:06.322
council or through a by election. Both options

03:06.386 --> 03:10.098
are highlighted in the report itself. If you have any

03:10.154 --> 03:13.938
questions for us about specifically about the application process. Tim Brubacher,

03:13.954 --> 03:17.442
our deputy Clerk, has been working on all of the research and

03:17.466 --> 03:21.202
information for that, so he'll be happy to answer those questions. And at this point,

03:21.226 --> 03:24.110
we'll just open up the floor for debater questions. Thank you.

03:24.730 --> 03:26.550
Thank you. Councillor Vrbanovic,

03:28.490 --> 03:32.466
thank you very much. And thank you to staff for bringing

03:32.498 --> 03:35.470
this comprehensive report forward.

03:36.090 --> 03:39.842
I guess just a couple questions, because I think it's

03:39.906 --> 03:45.778
worthwhile reiterating them here, even though I recognize they're

03:45.794 --> 03:49.026
in the report. But the last time

03:49.178 --> 03:54.068
we were faced with this, I recall, was with Councillor Clark

03:54.164 --> 03:57.748
when the late Wayne Wetlaufer passed

03:57.764 --> 04:01.060
away. Can you remind us what we

04:01.100 --> 04:04.276
did at that time? Did we go to the next person in the list or

04:04.348 --> 04:08.532
how did we do that through

04:08.556 --> 04:11.988
the chair in, I believe it was 2015, when Councillor Wetlaufer passed

04:12.004 --> 04:15.620
away. Elizabeth Clark was selected at the time, and she was

04:15.660 --> 04:19.136
the fifth place candidate in the previous election.

04:19.308 --> 04:23.400
Okay, thank you for that. And in

04:23.440 --> 04:27.304
terms of. In the report, you reference Mr.

04:27.352 --> 04:31.060
Rodriguez, who I'll note is in the. In the audience today.

04:32.800 --> 04:36.984
I'm just wondering, have you had an opportunity to confer

04:37.032 --> 04:42.600
with him and confirm whether or not he would be available through

04:42.640 --> 04:45.944
the Chair? Yes, we have spoken with Mr. Rodriguez on a

04:45.952 --> 04:49.844
couple of occasions, and he has indicated that he is still eligible

04:49.892 --> 04:53.044
and would be willing to serve should council appoint him.

04:53.132 --> 04:56.548
Okay. If that's the will of council,

04:56.724 --> 05:00.004
we would confirm with Mr.

05:00.052 --> 05:03.284
Rodriguez that he still has a qualifying address, but that would

05:03.292 --> 05:06.244
be what we would need to do on our end. Okay, thank you.

05:06.332 --> 05:09.732
Thank you for that. So, Madam Chair, at the appropriate

05:09.876 --> 05:14.170
time, I would like to move a motion and.

05:14.210 --> 05:16.070
And speak to it at that time, please.

05:17.570 --> 05:21.482
Councillor Foxton. Thank you,

05:21.506 --> 05:24.698
Madam Chair. I.

05:24.754 --> 05:29.002
I feel that it's too close to the next election to go into an election.

05:29.186 --> 05:31.190
I. I don't want to spend the money.

05:32.610 --> 05:36.410
I don't think it's a wise thing. And I think the next in line

05:36.450 --> 05:39.700
was very close to the previous person that won it.

05:39.850 --> 05:43.280
And so I'm leaning towards going that route, especially since

05:43.320 --> 05:47.408
the individual was already involved in the community extensively

05:47.504 --> 05:50.768
before the election. And that was one of the reasons I believe,

05:50.824 --> 05:54.512
he wanted to run again. I know that it's in

05:54.536 --> 05:58.128
the report, but. Tim, do you want to tell us what the differential was

05:58.184 --> 06:01.632
between Mr. Deutschmann's results and the

06:01.656 --> 06:04.912
next on the line? Thank you,

06:04.936 --> 06:09.580
Chair. So Councillor Deutschmann received 10,102 votes,

06:09.760 --> 06:13.572
and Mr. Rodriguez received 9,714

06:13.676 --> 06:17.316
votes. And that's fewer

06:17.348 --> 06:20.800
than 400. Thank you,

06:21.180 --> 06:24.548
Councillor Huinink. Thank you, Chair. I would agree

06:24.604 --> 06:29.844
very strongly that the voice of the people spoke when they chose

06:29.972 --> 06:33.748
Mr. Rodriguez's fifth. And it would be in Council's best interest

06:33.884 --> 06:38.144
to bring him on as quickly as possible, also to proceed

06:38.192 --> 06:41.504
with the necessary engagements of Council

06:41.672 --> 06:43.020
as soon as we can.

06:46.040 --> 06:49.792
Thank you, Councillor Salonen. Thank you.

06:49.816 --> 06:53.312
Through you, Chair, I think I share a lot of the similar sentiment

06:53.376 --> 06:56.832
that's been discussed. Looking at Mr.

06:56.896 --> 07:00.864
Rodriguez and the position, I think certainly from a democratic

07:00.912 --> 07:04.390
process, he's someone who's already gone out to the public, shown his

07:04.430 --> 07:08.230
interest in this role. And again, it was actually quite close.

07:08.350 --> 07:10.838
So I think from a cost savings perspective,

07:10.934 --> 07:14.982
from getting the right people in the position, I think

07:15.166 --> 07:18.134
that's the route I would like to see go. And I'd be happy to Second.

07:18.222 --> 07:21.702
I'm assuming that's what Councillor Verbanovic was

07:21.726 --> 07:22.690
going to bring forward.

07:26.510 --> 07:29.734
Okay. I probably should have asked Councillor Vrbanovic

07:29.782 --> 07:32.678
to put his motion forward. There is no motion on the floor at this point,

07:32.734 --> 07:36.074
so I am going to go the Speaker's list and we are not.

07:36.222 --> 07:39.730
Any motion. I think it's pretty clear what the sentiment is around

07:39.770 --> 07:43.790
the Horseshoe, but there's no motion on the floor. Councillor Erb, Council member,

07:48.010 --> 07:51.570
I indicated that at the appropriate time, I'd like to move a motion.

07:51.650 --> 07:54.770
So is this the appropriate time or.

07:54.890 --> 07:57.810
I have a Speaker's list. So I will go back. I'll come back to you,

07:57.850 --> 08:01.026
Councillor Erb. Thank you,

08:01.098 --> 08:03.986
Madam Chair. I too,

08:04.138 --> 08:08.766
support making an appointment. I think Councillor

08:08.798 --> 08:12.398
Deutschmann had the 10,000 and the 9,000 for Mr.

08:12.414 --> 08:16.238
Rodriguez. But Councillor Deutschmann had 10% of the vote and

08:16.374 --> 08:19.918
Mr. Rodriguez had 9% of the vote. So it was obvious that the citizens

08:19.934 --> 08:23.950
of Kitchener put their faith almost equally

08:24.110 --> 08:27.614
into Mr. Rodriguez as they did to other councillor members.

08:27.702 --> 08:30.926
And we're more than halfway through the term.

08:30.998 --> 08:34.250
I don't see the necessity of

08:34.870 --> 08:38.782
a costly by election when we know that the

08:38.806 --> 08:42.490
candidate that considering appointing had

08:42.530 --> 08:46.710
that kind of support from the citizens of Kitchener. So I would assuming that

08:47.090 --> 08:50.618
Councillor Vrbanovic is going to make a motion

08:50.634 --> 08:54.122
to appoint Mr. Rodriguez, I would support that as

08:54.146 --> 08:57.306
well. Thank you, Councillor James.

08:57.418 --> 09:02.186
Thank you. Through you, Chair, I strongly

09:02.218 --> 09:06.202
support moving to the

09:06.226 --> 09:10.390
fifth individual. Mr. Rodriguez. I will speak to

09:10.690 --> 09:15.318
something that Councillor Huinink said as well. The community did

09:15.454 --> 09:18.710
put their their votes in Mr. Rodriguez, and he came in

09:18.750 --> 09:22.774
fifth. And based on precedent from before, I think there's ample

09:22.822 --> 09:26.310
reason to appoint the next person. We'll also just ask

09:26.350 --> 09:30.406
for clarification. What would be the cost of a

09:30.478 --> 09:33.334
by election or going through the other process?

09:33.422 --> 09:36.966
Just so that's clear. Thank. We'll go to Will.

09:37.038 --> 09:40.582
Yeah. Thank you, Councillor James. It would be approximately $800,000 to

09:40.606 --> 09:43.332
run a by election in Kitchener. Okay.

09:43.396 --> 09:46.884
And that from a. From a cost savings perspective,

09:46.932 --> 09:50.484
I Think it wouldn't make sense. So happy to

09:50.652 --> 09:54.484
support if there is a pending motion that will come forward on appointing

09:54.532 --> 09:58.040
the next person in line. Councillor Wolf,

09:59.100 --> 10:02.964
through you, Madam Chair, so far I agree with all my colleagues.

10:03.092 --> 10:07.060
I think to spend $800,000 on

10:07.100 --> 10:10.416
an election at this point would not be appropriate.

10:10.528 --> 10:13.936
And also that would leave us with an empty seat

10:14.048 --> 10:18.048
until June. So I've only heard good things about

10:18.184 --> 10:22.496
the delegate. And I think, as other colleagues

10:22.528 --> 10:26.048
have said, he did receive many votes

10:26.144 --> 10:29.232
from his constituents in Kitchener,

10:29.376 --> 10:32.480
and we do have to trust the electorate.

10:32.640 --> 10:37.024
And I again think the appointing

10:37.152 --> 10:40.840
of the next in line from the ballot would be our best choice.

10:41.740 --> 10:45.588
Councillor McCabe, thank you.

10:45.724 --> 10:50.000
I'll play a little bit of devil's advocate because I'm curious about.

10:50.620 --> 10:53.652
I'm actually more interested in doing some interviews,

10:53.716 --> 10:57.140
quite frankly, because I think that would. I think two and a half years have

10:57.180 --> 11:00.852
passed and there's a lot of issues that we've discussed and

11:00.876 --> 11:03.332
a lot of things that have changed in our community in two and a half

11:03.356 --> 11:07.084
years and that are going to continue to change in a. I personally would prefer

11:07.132 --> 11:10.236
to just open it up and look for. Not to run a by election,

11:10.308 --> 11:14.480
but my interest was really in soliciting

11:15.060 --> 11:20.092
interested applicants from across the community and

11:20.116 --> 11:23.400
then actually go through the time and see who would actually.

11:23.860 --> 11:27.340
Who actually rises to the top. Because two and a half years, nearly three years

11:27.380 --> 11:30.700
have passed, that actually would be my

11:30.740 --> 11:33.530
preference. And I know some other.

11:33.660 --> 11:37.182
Like the Catholic school board has done a process like that, and it brought in

11:37.206 --> 11:39.982
some more racialized candidates as well through that process.

11:40.086 --> 11:43.726
So that was one of my interests in opening

11:43.758 --> 11:45.530
it up to an interview process.

11:47.190 --> 11:51.210
So, yeah, that's how I feel about it. But I also just.

11:52.630 --> 11:56.126
And I'm not sure who could answer

11:56.158 --> 12:00.094
this, but I am concerned that he's currently

12:00.182 --> 12:03.790
employed by a municipality. So I think that's

12:03.950 --> 12:07.030
something that we need to consider as well in this process.

12:10.050 --> 12:13.338
Okay, Tim's going to respond to that question, so thank you.

12:13.394 --> 12:17.290
Chair. So the. The municipal act does not allow an

12:17.330 --> 12:21.350
employee of the municipality to serve on the council.

12:22.130 --> 12:25.674
So Mr. Rodriguez would not be allowed to be an employee of

12:25.682 --> 12:29.386
the. Or, sorry, a councillor at the city of Kitchener. But we're

12:29.418 --> 12:32.760
a different municipality, so that's. That's not covered. However,

12:32.800 --> 12:36.552
in our conversations with Mr. Rodriguez, he didn't

12:36.616 --> 12:40.008
indicate that he would be intending to take a leave of absence from his position

12:40.144 --> 12:44.420
at the city. And we also informed him that

12:44.800 --> 12:48.360
should this be the option that council chooses, that we would put

12:48.400 --> 12:52.040
him in touch with the integrity Commissioner to make

12:52.080 --> 12:56.232
sure that he was fully briefed on the

12:56.256 --> 13:00.232
implications as far as the Municipal Conflict of Interest act goes to

13:00.256 --> 13:03.496
avoid any issues there. Councillor McCabe.

13:03.608 --> 13:06.952
No, that's fine. I just think it's something that we should keep in our

13:06.976 --> 13:10.088
minds as we go through this process. I want to thank

13:10.104 --> 13:13.688
you for asking that question, though, because I think it's really important information for

13:13.824 --> 13:17.784
anybody who's watching this to know the commitment

13:17.832 --> 13:21.860
of the person we're talking about and also clarity on the path forward.

13:22.480 --> 13:25.576
I don't see any other speakers, so I will go back to Councillor

13:25.608 --> 13:28.580
Vrbanovic. Is there anyone who hasn't spoken that would like to.

13:29.670 --> 13:33.342
Okay, Councillor Vrbanovic, thank you. Thank you

13:33.366 --> 13:36.542
very much. Chair Redman and I

13:36.566 --> 13:40.014
will be moving Matt Rodriguez to fill

13:40.062 --> 13:44.702
the vacancy as

13:44.726 --> 13:48.558
a result of the vacancy created by former

13:48.614 --> 13:52.382
Councillor Deutschmann. And as has,

13:52.486 --> 13:56.302
I guess, already been offered. Councillor Salonen will second it. And if I

13:56.326 --> 13:58.930
can just speak to it briefly,

14:01.100 --> 14:04.532
as has been pointed out, we are a little more than

14:04.636 --> 14:08.084
two years past the last election,

14:08.252 --> 14:11.800
but when we're faced with these openings,

14:12.140 --> 14:15.956
obviously there are a number of options that are available to councils.

14:15.988 --> 14:19.940
But I think there are a couple principles that always need to be considered

14:20.020 --> 14:23.652
as we look at that. One is what were the results in

14:23.676 --> 14:28.040
the last election? And as has been pointed out, in this particular instance

14:28.400 --> 14:31.912
there was really only a gap of three hundred and eighty eight votes

14:31.976 --> 14:34.872
between the fourth and the fifth place person,

14:35.056 --> 14:38.648
which was very different than, for example, the sixth

14:38.744 --> 14:42.300
place, where there was actually a gap of almost 3,000 votes,

14:42.960 --> 14:45.992
which in that case, quite frankly,

14:46.136 --> 14:49.300
I think the circumstances and the discussion might be different

14:50.000 --> 14:53.432
because it's not clear that there

14:53.456 --> 14:56.632
was a very obvious next person in

14:56.656 --> 15:00.320
the list. So that's one

15:00.360 --> 15:03.408
reason why I think it makes sense to go this route.

15:03.584 --> 15:08.640
Secondly, obviously going the second or

15:08.680 --> 15:11.952
probably the most democratic route, which would have been going to a

15:11.976 --> 15:15.632
by election at a cost of $800,000 at

15:15.656 --> 15:19.328
this point in time, when there's an obvious person

15:19.384 --> 15:22.860
that was fifth in the list, in my view

15:23.160 --> 15:26.448
would not be a prudent use of taxpayers dollars,

15:26.544 --> 15:30.156
particularly at this time when we we're facing fiscal

15:30.188 --> 15:32.440
challenges as a region.

15:33.060 --> 15:36.972
Thirdly, I will say that going

15:37.156 --> 15:40.508
the route of appointment is an option available to us.

15:40.644 --> 15:42.880
Appointment by virtue of application.

15:43.540 --> 15:47.116
But it is one that I think brings

15:47.148 --> 15:50.620
me some concern, quite frankly, because it

15:50.660 --> 15:53.932
doesn't necessarily allow for the voice of

15:53.956 --> 15:57.820
the people of Kitchener to be heard. Number one, we could

15:57.860 --> 16:01.000
see anybody applying from within

16:01.680 --> 16:05.340
the region, which people are allowed to do that. But secondly,

16:05.920 --> 16:09.416
it doesn't allow for Kitchener voters

16:09.528 --> 16:13.256
to have their say. Except for the four of us

16:13.408 --> 16:17.240
around the Horseshoe that are actually Kitchener voters. Actually there's five,

16:17.280 --> 16:21.192
I guess, because Councillor Huinink is

16:21.216 --> 16:24.060
a Kitchener resident representing Waterloo.

16:24.560 --> 16:28.328
And so I think in the principles

16:28.424 --> 16:32.488
of. In the principle of democracy,

16:32.584 --> 16:37.720
in the principle of acknowledging the

16:37.760 --> 16:41.400
votes that took place recently. And I will argue that, as is

16:41.440 --> 16:45.448
pointed out, Mr. Rodriguez has indicated,

16:45.544 --> 16:49.272
in my view, his commitment to serving on council with

16:49.296 --> 16:52.024
his willingness to take the leave, as Mr.

16:52.072 --> 16:55.576
Brubacher indicated, despite the Municipal

16:55.608 --> 16:59.392
act not requiring that. But he does have

16:59.416 --> 17:03.248
extensive municipal experience which I think will help

17:03.304 --> 17:07.184
him as he comes around the Horseshoe to

17:07.352 --> 17:09.660
work with us for the balance of this term.

17:10.920 --> 17:14.624
Councillor Salonen, did you want to make any comments as the seconder of

17:14.632 --> 17:17.660
this motion? Thank you. I think I already made my comments.

17:19.880 --> 17:23.216
So, Matt, this is how smooth it runs. Every time we have a council

17:23.288 --> 17:26.732
meeting. So it's been moved and

17:26.756 --> 17:30.236
seconded to the regional municipality of Waterloo selects

17:30.348 --> 17:34.364
A1 option 1A. And the associated process

17:34.452 --> 17:38.172
is outlined in the report dated March 4, 2025 as

17:38.196 --> 17:41.680
a method for filling the vacant regional councilor,

17:42.100 --> 17:45.820
the Kitchener seat. So I would ask everybody to please

17:45.860 --> 17:51.140
use your E scribe to vote.

18:09.310 --> 18:13.366
That is carried. Colleagues, I would then turn to Tim Brubacher

18:13.398 --> 18:17.558
to talk about the way forward. Thank you, Chair Redman.

18:17.654 --> 18:21.490
So when the report was written, the timeline that

18:21.530 --> 18:25.042
we have included in appendix A notes that a

18:25.066 --> 18:29.874
bylaw will come to confirm Mr.

18:29.922 --> 18:33.474
Rodriguez's appointment at the 19th

18:33.522 --> 18:37.666
council meeting. Given that there is a special council meeting called

18:37.818 --> 18:41.922
for the 13th, we would suggest that this just

18:41.946 --> 18:45.250
be added to the purpose for that meeting and the bylaw can be

18:45.370 --> 18:48.666
passed at that point. Sounds like

18:48.738 --> 18:52.554
a great solution and a little bit of clarity on the way forward.

18:52.722 --> 18:56.122
And Matt, I guess my reflection would be

18:56.146 --> 18:59.626
that none of these seats have seat belts in them, but you're joining regional council

18:59.698 --> 19:03.642
at a very crucial, interesting time in the history of the region.

19:03.746 --> 19:06.790
So we look forward to having you around the Horseshoe with all of us.

19:08.130 --> 19:11.354
Colleagues, I will now entertain a motion to

19:11.362 --> 19:14.682
go into closed. If I could have a movement moved by Councillor Wolf, seconded by

19:14.706 --> 19:25.538
Councillor Foxton. It's to issues

19:25.594 --> 19:29.362
in a court. So it's receiving advice that is subject to solicitor

19:29.426 --> 19:33.390
client privilege receiving advice subject to

19:35.690 --> 19:39.570
solicitor client privilege receiving advice related to

19:39.610 --> 19:43.250
proposed disposition of land, the impact of terrorists,

19:43.330 --> 19:47.314
identifiable individuals and a proposed acquisition

19:47.362 --> 19:50.330
of land in the city of Cambridge.

20:13.960 --> 20:16.820
Harris, McCabe and Salonen, if you could vote,

20:20.520 --> 20:24.080
colleagues, that is carried. We will now adjourn to the

20:24.120 --> 20:25.260
Waterloo Room.

20:39.090 --> 01:41:47.158
It colleagues,

